# Copy to studio/.env and fill in whichever backends you use.
# studio/.env is gitignored and is never read by anything but the local server.
# A variable already exported in your shell takes precedence over this file.

# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=...

# --- Jev: experimental native CAD workflows; no extra SDK ----------------
# Get a key at https://console.typesafe.ai/keys
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=...
# Select the Jev preset in Studio, or replace STUDIO_PROVIDER/STUDIO_MODEL
# below with jev / jev-1.13.0. Jev never invokes STUDIO_VISION_MODEL.

# --- Hybrid: Astra plans, code executes, Jev chooses only when needed ----
# Authenticate/update Codex CLI; then select the hybrid preset, or set:
# STUDIO_PROVIDER=hybrid
# STUDIO_MODEL=gpt-6-astra
# STUDIO_HYBRID_JEV_MODEL=jev-1.13.0
# To explicitly permit missing-tool implementation, use STUDIO_PROVIDER=hybrid_dev
# instead, or select “Astra + Jev · tool building (source edits)” in Studio.
# This grants trusted Python development/testing permission; it is not a sandbox.
# Uses TYPESAFE_API_KEY above only for explicit choice steps. Astra planning
# ignores the normal full-auto Codex/MCP configuration and returns JSON plans.

# --- OpenRouter: one key, every model, per-call billing -------------------
# openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# The pairing: a cheap worker to drive the tools, a strong model to look at
# captures. The vision call carries no conversation history, so it stays
# around $0.006 a session even on a good model -- pick it for quality.
STUDIO_PROVIDER=openrouter
STUDIO_MODEL=z-ai/glm-5.3-flash
STUDIO_VISION_PROVIDER=openrouter
STUDIO_VISION_MODEL=z-ai/glm-5.3-flash
